FIX 1 render_sender v1 rate: v1 frames now go on a heap drained by one `_Releaser` thread (owns the StreamClient sends, releases in t_release = t_state + latency[stream] order, counts `late`); the 30 Hz render tick never sleeps. test_v1_render_stream hardened: receiver fps_in >= 27 and inter-arrival p95 <= 50 ms on both streams, stamp error p95 <= 10 ms kept, ready-file fps within 10 % of measured. Before (review): fps_in 13.97, inter-arrival p50 78.5 ms. After: fps_in 29.9/29.9, inter-arrival p95 40.3 ms, stamp error p95 2.3/2.4 ms, late 0-1 of 422 sent. test_render_sender.py: v1 passes 6/6 runs under the lock. v2 flaked once (stamp error p95 1.84 ms > 1 ms limit, errors drift 0.9 -> 1.2 ms, another job was using the machine); passes at 0.37 ms otherwise (see rerun line below).
TAG OFFSET cause (investigated, extension_m is NOT ignored): tags and both cameras are rigid in the TCP frame (C_T_TCP measured; the pad centre = TCP height moves with extension_m), so the tag position in the UW image cannot depend on the finger extension: identical camera-check tag error for 0.0 and +0.1 m is correct by construction. The real error was in the tag placement relative to the TCP: (a) model.py put the tag at the pad centre height (TCP, ~211 mm from the camera along z); the real tags are ~98 mm from the UW camera (iPhUMI gripper_calibration artag_z_distance_from_ultrawide 0.098079): dz = -108 mm along TCP z reproduces the whole UW-frame offset (0, +23, -104) mm (y by the 15 deg camera tilt). (b) after (a) a constant lateral error remained: sim tag separation = gap + 24 mm, real = zarr width + 44 mm = gap + 87 mm (sim_minus_real -62.3 mm, p95 -62.2, spread 0.1 mm over widths 45-84 mm): tags 31.2 mm further out per side.
 Fix (model.py, Track A): TAG_Z_FROM_PAD_M = -0.108 and TAG_Y_EXTRA_M = 0.0312 (overridable via tooling.finger_adapter.tag_z_from_pad_m / tag_y_extra_m; both independent of extension_m). Tests (test_model.py, +6): tag depth in UW = 0.098 +- 12 mm and tag z in TCP frame == TAG_Z_FROM_PAD_M for panda/fr3 x extension 0.0/0.1; tag separation = gap + 87 mm +- 2 mm for panda/fr3.
 Result (5 demos x 40 frames): offset UW mm id0/id1 (-14.6,+23.0,-103.9)/(47.8,18.5,-104.2) -> (16.65,-5.0,0.4)/(16.63,-9.5,0.1); separation sim-minus-real -62.3 -> +0.15 mm; tag px p50 129.8/178.3 -> 43.9/48.6.
 Remaining ~46 px = UW extrinsic placeholder (12 mm along +y). Translation-only fit now gives C_main_T_C_uw t = (-0.016643, +0.019263, -0.000265) m (px p50 46.3 -> 9.7; 6-DoF 8.3 px, rot 2.6 deg). TRACK B / config change (not done here): set tooling.C_main_T_C_uw in configs/station/tooling/franka_hand_iphumi_iphone16pro.yaml to identity rotation with that translation (iPhone only; the rig UW is a virtual camera, its extrinsic comes from the rig calibration). UW_PLACEHOLDER in model.py left unchanged because the rig profile shares it.
FIX 4 render realism (cheap, Track A only): render.DEFAULT_COLORS (table grey 0.30, eraser yellow-green, backdrop grey) and a visual-only floor plane "backdrop" 0.70 m below the table top in model.py (contype/conaffinity 0, no physics effect) so past the table edge the image is not black. Main plain MAE full 93.4 -> 59.8, UW 99.9 -> 67.9 (ext set); SSIM main 0.34 -> 0.57. Not fitted to those numbers; colours picked from the look of the real frames.
KNOWN LIMITATION (render realism): roi MAE still ~100 (fingers/tags/eraser region) and UW SSIM 0.41. Remaining differences: (1) eraser size: configs/station/scene/block_raise_table.yaml has a 60x20x12 mm placeholder, the real eraser in the main frame is clearly larger (measure it; Track B config); (2) the sim fingers are two 20x8x30 mm pads, real ones are long white printed fingers with a ribbed flat face and the tags on wings; (3) the table/floor/wall are flat colours, the real scene has texture, a bag, a wall; (4) lighting is flat, no soft shadows. Proposed fix order: eraser dimensions and colour from the scene yaml, then printed-finger mesh (CAD or a measured box set with the tag wings), then a textured table plane and a wall/floor backdrop. Until closed, render-based Stage 3 success is INFORMATIONAL: camera-gap (ext set, panda, 24 queries, 20 predicted) render_both pos gap vs real k15 p50/p95 32.7/75.0 mm, roi_paste 12.0/30.3 mm.
